%% Sequence — scheduled scan (cron, full/active profile)
%% Canonical source. Regenerate exports with: npm run docs:diagrams
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CRON as scheduled-scans.yml (daily cron)
    participant ENQ as enqueue-scheduled-scans.ts
    participant DB as Supabase
    participant M as Worker matrix (shards)
    participant TOOLS as Real tool binaries + ZAP daemon
    participant FEEDS as OSV / NVD / KEV / EPSS / crt.sh
    participant N as Notifiers

    CRON->>ENQ: run enqueue step
    ENQ->>DB: for each verified target, isScanDue(plan)?
    Note right of ENQ: Basic weekly, Pro/Agency daily
    ENQ->>DB: INSERT one scan_jobs row per due target

    CRON->>M: start worker shard matrix
    CRON->>TOOLS: install nmap/nuclei/sqlmap/commix/testssl/gitleaks/trivy/opengrep + ZAP
    loop until queue drained or time budget (MAX_JOBS_PER_RUN)
        M->>DB: claim_scan_job() SKIP LOCKED
        M->>M: decideScanConfig() -> profile (default "full")
        M->>TOOLS: base passive + extended active tools
        TOOLS->>FEEDS: CVE / exploit / CT lookups
        M->>DB: write results, status=completed
        M->>DB: finding_lifecycle + SLA sync, New/Fixed diff
        M->>N: webhooks, Slack/Teams, email, on-call, SIEM
        M->>N: attack-surface + emerging-threat + lookalike alerts
        M->>N: ticket dedupe + auto-close
    end
    Note over M,DB: leftover jobs roll over to the next cron run
